// Title: Process Monitor Driver Creation By Non-Sysinternals Binary
// Sigma ID: a05baa88-e922-4001-bc4d-8738135f27de
// Status: test | Level: medium
// Author: Nasreddine Bencherchali (Nextron Systems)
// Date: 2023-05-05 | Modified: 2026-06-29
// ATT&CK: persistence, privilege-escalation, T1068
// Description: Detects creation of the Process Monitor driver by processes other than Process Monitor (procmon)
//   itself.
// False positives:
//   - Some false positives may occur with legitimate renamed process monitor binaries
// References:
//   - Internal Research
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/adf5a626c4a776f3f023056f0f398b9523a2f09e/rules/windows/file/file_event/file_event_win_sysinternals_procmon_driver_susp_creation.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language 12.4.1, live Defender schema)
// Machine-generated and not tested against real telemetry. Verify before use as a detection.

DeviceFileEvents
| where (FolderPath contains "\\procmon" and FolderPath endswith ".sys") and (not((InitiatingProcessFolderPath endswith "\\procmon.exe" or InitiatingProcessFolderPath endswith "\\procmon64.exe" or InitiatingProcessFolderPath endswith "\\procmon64a.exe")))
